<p><img src="https://cdn3.brettterpstra.com/uploads/2026/10/zombie-nvalt-rb.7539.png" width="800" height="226" style="margin:0 auto;clear:both;" class="header" /></p>
<p>While the world waits for <a href="https://nvultra.com">nvUltra</a> to finish its years-long beta, I&rsquo;m updating nvALT to keep things running until I can offer the viable alternative. Appropriate to the season, nvALT is rising from the grave. Braiiiins!</p>

<p>Brains, in all seriousness, because nvALT became a second brain for a lot of people. Myself included. I&rsquo;ve been using nvUltra instead for years now, but it&rsquo;s not publicly available yet and I left a lot of people in the lurch. I&rsquo;m going to be using nvALT and nvUltra in the same sentences a bit in this post, so you might have to train yourself to read: nvALT == old version, nvUltra == upcoming (unreleased) new version.</p>

<p><img src="https://cdn3.brettterpstra.com/uploads/2026/10/nvAlt-icon.png"></p>
<p>If you don&rsquo;t want the whole story, <a href="https://brettterpstra.com#dl">skip to the download</a>. Note that because of all the changes I had to make it compile for Apple Silicon, the old auto-update won&rsquo;t work. You have to download 3.0 directly, and after that updates will function normally.</p>

<h3 id="backstory">Backstory</h3>

<p>The original Notational Velocity is also seeing updates for the first time in years right now, so I was encouraged to get nvALT modernized. nvUltra, to me, is a far superior app, and I&rsquo;m not hesitant to keep nvALT running for now &mdash; I&rsquo;m convinced users interested in the improvements in nvUltra will be willing to pay for it.</p>

<p>So I&rsquo;ve been modernizing the codebase and making it compile and run on Apple Silicon. I brought in upstream fixes from Notational Velocity. Switched it from the old Multimarkdown processor to a new build of Apex. Fixed some editing issues. Removed Peggd and added Marked Share publishing.</p>

<p>I&rsquo;m not setting up Marked Share as a full SimpleNote replacement in nvALT quite yet. Marked Share is ready to handle it, at least as far as the API goes, but a couple hundred thousand notes might cost me more to run than I&rsquo;m prepared to pay before I start charging anything for it. So for now it just works as one-off publishing and sharing, not a full online sync/backup. That may evolve.</p>

<p>nvALT predated my <a href="https://brettterpstra.com/projects/howzit/">Howzit</a> build notes system, so putting the pieces back together and rebuilding the publishing pipeline was somewhat painstaking. Hopefully I got it all right. And it&rsquo;s all documented in my build notes for the future.</p>

<p>I went ahead and made a simple Icon Composer icon for it. It&rsquo;s not nearly as cool as the old nvALT icon, but that one didn&rsquo;t look great in the Squircle and I needed something that still looked up-to-date in the Dock.</p>

<p>If you&rsquo;ve been a long-time nvALT user, this update is for you. I&rsquo;m not trying to add a bunch of new users at this point, but I&rsquo;m also not trying to avoid it, so do what you will. If you&rsquo;ve been using it, though, and I inadvertently broke a feature you&rsquo;d come to rely on, please let me know. You can <a href="https://brettterpstra.com/contact/">contact me directly</a> or post an issue <a href="https://github.com/ttscof/nv/issues">on GitHub</a>.</p>

<p>Like I said, nvUltra is a complete rewrite, with <em>way</em> better Markdown features and preview, multiple notebooks, subfolders, and a whole lot more. When the time comes (shooting for 2026 still), I think folks will switch over.</p>

<h3 id="changelog">Changelog</h3>

<h4 id="changed">CHANGED</h4>

<ul>
  <li>nvALT now requires <strong>macOS 12</strong> or later.</li>
  <li><strong>Check for Updates</strong> works again on current macOS, using Sparkle 2 and the existing designheresy feed.</li>
  <li><strong>MultiMarkdown preview</strong> is rendered by Apex instead of the bundled multimarkdown tool.</li>
  <li>Preview <strong>Share</strong> publishes the note to Marked Share instead of Peggd and copies an unlisted link.</li>
  <li><strong>Note text and the note list</strong> use the regular system font size. Existing Helvetica 12 notes and the old 11 or 12 point list size are updated once.</li>
  <li><strong>Note list headers</strong> are flat, with a hairline separator and a chevron for the sorted column.</li>
  <li>The <strong>search field</strong> no longer draws its old horizontal border lines.</li>
  <li>Replace the preview <strong>Save HTML</strong> button with <strong>Open in Marked</strong> for plain text notes stored on disk.</li>
  <li>Turn on <strong>Markdown</strong> shortcuts by default, so Command-B and Command-I insert syntax instead of rich text.</li>
  <li>Use the new <strong>app icon</strong>, including the Icon Composer icon on current macOS and a generated icon for older systems.</li>
  <li>Store new note databases as <strong>plain text</strong> files instead of a single database. Existing database-only libraries stay as they are.</li>
  <li>Use <strong>md</strong> as the default extension for plain text notes, including libraries that were using txt, text, or utf8. A custom extension is left as the default.</li>
  <li>Store note <strong>tags</strong> as Finder tags. Existing OpenMeta tags on note files are copied over on launch, and later edits stay in Finder.</li>
</ul>

<h4 id="new">NEW</h4>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Open Marked Streaming Preview</strong> sends the current note to Marked and opens x-marked://stream/. It is in the Preview menu and the status menu.</li>
  <li>Highlight <strong>Markdown</strong> syntax in the editor while Markdown completion is on.</li>
  <li>Ask once, on launch, whether to convert a <strong>Rich Text</strong> library to Markdown.</li>
  <li>Add <strong>Convert to Markdown</strong> in Notes settings. Rich Text notes are converted, plain text notes are copied as they are, and the files are written into a new folder that then becomes the notes folder. The current folder is left unchanged.</li>
</ul>

<h4 id="improved">IMPROVED</h4>

<ul>
  <li>nvALT runs natively on <strong>Apple silicon</strong> as well as Intel.</li>
  <li><strong>Web links</strong> in notes are found by the system link detector. Double-bracket wiki links still work.</li>
  <li><strong>Encrypted notes</strong> still open. Crypto now uses the system libraries instead of the bundled OpenSSL.</li>
  <li>nvALT uses standard Finder tags instead of OpenMeta tags when syncing to Finder</li>
</ul>

<h4 id="fixed">FIXED</h4>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Typing in a note</strong> no longer crashes if the text gets shorter during an edit.</li>
  <li>The <strong>password generator</strong> no longer stalls when the length is longer than the character set.</li>
  <li>Make the <strong>Marked Share</strong> confirmation follow light and dark mode and show its buttons.</li>
  <li>Pressing <strong>Return</strong> on an empty continued list item removes the marker and leaves a blank line.</li>
</ul>

